findings.citation_text:
4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
1) under equipment on food and drink service counters (dust/food debris); 
2) bottom inside storage cooler (food/general debris; splash);
3) bottom inside storage freezer (food/general debris);  and
4) cabinet doors and inner surfaces at food and drink service counters (splash).
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.

findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) cabinets with drains for soda and Fizzfreeze machines, especially around the Fizzfreeze drain (splash and dead drain flies);
B) bottom inside reach-in freezer, ledge of grated cover, and along bottom of gasket (food debris/splash);
C) ledge of grated cover on 2 door cooler (splash);
D) front counter cooler - bottom inside and gasket (debris);
E) under rollers and condiment holder (dust/debris);
F) cabinet under handsink at food counter (buildup);
G) garbage can storage cabinets (splash/debris);
H) cabinets below cappuccino machines (powder/buildup);
I) counter under cappuccino machines (powder/dust);
J) Island Freeze machine - underneath surfaces and water lines (syrup buildup);  and
K) organizer for coffee/tea creamers and sugars (general debris).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

findings.citation_text:
750.1200 & 1220 - A) Plastic baseboard was loose along the floor to wall juncture behind the soda syrup boxes (beneath back side of soda machines). Re-attach the loose base board.

B) Floors were soiled in the following areas with debris and/or splash:
1. under shelves in alcohol walkin (members only area);
2. under ice machine;
3. under 2 door cooler & reach-in freezer;
4. around soda syrup boxes;   and
5. walkin coolers - under shelves and beneath doors of the reach-in sections.
Clean the floors under equipment and throughout the facility daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

Floors must be in good repair, constructed to facilitate easy cleaning, and maintained clean. The junctures between walls and floors shall be coved and sealed.
